# ==========================================
# Notifications
# ==========================================

### Create First User
# @name createUser1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "johndoe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "securepassword123",
  "bio": "Software Engineer",
  "avatarUrl": "https://example.com/avatar1.jpg",
  "isPrivate": false
}

### Create Second User
# @name createUser2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "janedoe",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "password": "securepassword456",
  "bio": "Graphic Designer",
  "isPrivate": true
}

### Login First User
# @name loginUser1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

### Login Second User
# @name loginUser2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "password": "securepassword456"
}

# ==========================================
# Follow Notification
# ==========================================

### User1 follows User2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{createUser2.response.body.id}}/follow
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}

### Get User2 notifications
# @name user2Notifications
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### Get User2 unread notifications
# @name user2Unread
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/unread
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### Mark first notification as read
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/{{user2Unread.response.body.$[0].id}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

# ==========================================
# Comment and like notifications
# ==========================================

### Create Post for Comments
# @name createPost
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}

{
  "authorId": "{{createUser1.response.body.id}}",
  "content": "Post that will receive comments",
  "imageUrl": null,
  "visibility": "PUBLIC"
}

### Create Comment on Post
# @name createComment
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.id}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

{
  "authorId": "{{createUser2.response.body.id}}",
  "content": "Great post! Really enjoyed reading this."
}

### Check User1 notifications
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}

### User2 Likes Post
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.id}}/like?userId={{createUser2.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### Check User1 notifications
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}

### User1 Likes Comment1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.id}}/comments/{{createComment.response.body.id}}/like?userId={{createUser1.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}

### Check User2 notifications
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

# ==========================================
# Message notifications
# ==========================================

### User1 sends first message to User2
# @name sendMessage1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/messages/{{createUser2.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Hello Jane!"
}

### Check User2 notifications
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### User2 replies
# @name sendMessage2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/messages/{{createUser1.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Hi John!"
}

### Check User1 notifications
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}

# ==========================================
# Group notifications
# ==========================================

### User1 creates a group
# @name createGroup
POST http://localhost:8080/api/groups
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Group",
  "description": "Group used for notification testing"
}

### User1 invites User2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/groups/{{createGroup.response.body.id}}/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "inviteeId": "{{createUser2.response.body.id}}"
}

### User2 gets invitations
# @name getInvites
GET http://localhost:8080/api/groups/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### Check User2 notifications (should include invite)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### User2 accepts invitation
POST http://localhost:8080/api/groups/invitations/{{getInvites.response.body.$[0].id}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}
Content-Length: 0

### Check User1 notifications (invite accepted)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}

### Promote User2 to ADMIN
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/groups/{{createGroup.response.body.id}}/members/{{createUser2.response.body.id}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### Check User2 notifications (role change)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### Kick User2
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/groups/{{createGroup.response.body.id}}/members/{{createUser2.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}

### Check User2 notifications (kick notification)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### Delete the group
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/groups/{{createGroup.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}

### Check User2 notifications again
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### Mark All Notifications Read
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### Verify no unread notifications
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications/unread
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

# ==========================================
# Cleanup
# ==========================================

### Delete Second User
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/users/self
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser2.response.body.token}}

### Delete First User
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/users/self
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser1.response.body.token}}## Description
This PR fixes cascade deletion for comments and their associated likes,
and adds authorization checks when liking private posts.

### Bug Fix: Cascade Deletion
Previously, deleting a comment did not remove its associated likes from the
database, leaving orphaned `Like` documents in the `likes` collection.
Similarly, deleting a post did not properly cascade through comments' likes.

**Before:**
- Delete comment → comment removed, but likes on that comment remained
- Delete post → post and comments removed, but likes on comments remained

**After:**
- Delete comment → comment removed + all likes on that comment removed
- Delete post → post removed + all comments removed + all likes on post
  and on each comment removed

### New Feature: Private Post Like Authorization
Users can no longer like a private post unless they follow the author.
Attempting to do so returns `401 Unauthorized`.

**Rules:**
- PUBLIC posts → anyone can like
- PRIVATE posts → only the author or their followers can like
- Violating this returns `UnauthorizedException`

## Changes

### Cascade Deletion Fix
- Updated `PostService.deletePost()` to iterate through all comments
  and delete their associated likes before deleting the comments
- Updated `CommentService.deleteComment()` to delete all likes
  targeting the comment before deleting the comment itself

### Private Post Like Authorization
- Added private post visibility check in `LikeService.likePost()`
- Added `FollowRepository` dependency injection in `LikeService`
- Added `existsByFollowerIdAndFollowingId()` method in
  `FollowRepository`
- Added `UnauthorizedException` in `exception/`

## Files Changed
- `service/PostService.java` — cascade delete through comment likes
- `service/CommentService.java` — cascade delete comment likes
- `service/LikeService.java` — added private post check + follow repo
- `repository/FollowRepository.java` — added exists query method
- `exception/UnauthorizedException.java` — new exception (401)

## Testing

### Cascade Deletion
- Verified deleting a comment removes all its likes
- Verified deleting a post removes all comments AND all likes on
  those comments
- Verified no orphaned `Like` documents remain after deletion

### Private Post Like Authorization
- Verified liking a PUBLIC post works for any user
- Verified liking a PRIVATE post works for the author
- Verified liking a PRIVATE post works for a follower of the author
- Verified liking a PRIVATE post fails with `401 Unauthorized` for
  a non-follower
- Test coverage: ___%## Description
This PR fixes cascade deletion for comments and their associated likes,
and adds authorization checks when liking private posts.

### Bug Fix: Cascade Deletion
Previously, deleting a comment did not remove its associated likes from the
database, leaving orphaned `Like` documents in the `likes` collection.
Similarly, deleting a post did not properly cascade through comments' likes.

**Before:**
- Delete comment → comment removed, but likes on that comment remained
- Delete post → post and comments removed, but likes on comments remained

**After:**
- Delete comment → comment removed + all likes on that comment removed
- Delete post → post removed + all comments removed + all likes on post
  and on each comment removed

### New Feature: Private Post Like Authorization
Users can no longer like a private post unless they follow the author.
Attempting to do so returns `401 Unauthorized`.

**Rules:**
- PUBLIC posts → anyone can like
- PRIVATE posts → only the author or their followers can like
- Violating this returns `UnauthorizedException`

## Changes

### Cascade Deletion Fix
- Updated `PostService.deletePost()` to iterate through all comments
  and delete their associated likes before deleting the comments
- Updated `CommentService.deleteComment()` to delete all likes
  targeting the comment before deleting the comment itself

### Private Post Like Authorization
- Added private post visibility check in `LikeService.likePost()`
- Added `FollowRepository` dependency injection in `LikeService`
- Added `existsByFollowerIdAndFollowingId()` method in
  `FollowRepository`
- Added `UnauthorizedException` in `exception/`

## Files Changed
- `service/PostService.java` — cascade delete through comment likes
- `service/CommentService.java` — cascade delete comment likes
- `service/LikeService.java` — added private post check + follow repo
- `repository/FollowRepository.java` — added exists query method
- `exception/UnauthorizedException.java` — new exception (401)

## Testing

### Cascade Deletion
- Verified deleting a comment removes all its likes
- Verified deleting a post removes all comments AND all likes on
  those comments
- Verified no orphaned `Like` documents remain after deletion

### Private Post Like Authorization
- Verified liking a PUBLIC post works for any user
- Verified liking a PRIVATE post works for the author
- Verified liking a PRIVATE post works for a follower of the author
- Verified liking a PRIVATE post fails with `401 Unauthorized` for
  a non-follower
- Test coverage: ___%